# ============================================================================
# Patch 0002 - Team member reclaim: terminal `retired` phase + slot reclamation
# ============================================================================
#
# applies-to: deepseek-harness @ 296181d1c2 (branch `dev`)
#   This HEAD already contains patch 0001's per-teammate route work (landed as
#   b62215edfa); 0002 applies on top of it.
# base tree: clean working tree at 296181d1c2
#
# Aligned with docs/design/team-member-reclaim-solution.md (T3) P1 checklist,
# with ONE deliberate deviation required by the task brief: a `running` target
# is REJECTED with TEAM_MEMBER_RUNNING (interrupt first), instead of T3's
# "drain-running-inside-retire" option; the drain still runs before the durable
# tombstone for every non-running target.
#
# What it changes (11 files, +283/-23):
#   agent-team/src/types.ts
#     - TeamMemberPhase gains the terminal 'retired' value
#     - TeamMemberView['status'] gains 'retired'
#     - TeamMemberProjection.phase keeps the full union (retired rows are
#       tombstones, kept for task ownerName resolution and audit)
#     - team/member SessionEventMap version is now 2 | 3
#     - adds RetireTeammateResult; maxMembers doc means non-retired members
#   agent-team/src/projection.ts
#     - teamMemberSnapshotSchema + teamMemberProjectionSchema accept 'retired'
#     - teamMemberEventSchema accepts version 2 or 3
#     - state machine allows provisioning->active|failed and
#       active|failed->retired; retired is absorbing; every other edge rejected
#     - retired tombstones stay in the durable client view (no filter)
#     - projection cache stateVersion 4 -> 5
#   agent-team/src/roster.ts
#     - spawnAdmitted counts only non-retired members against maxMembers
#     - new retire(caller,targetName): Lead-only, rejects running/provisioning,
#       drains the child session first, then appends the durable 'retired'
#       tombstone with team/member version 3; a repeated call is an idempotent
#       no-op; names stay permanently reserved
#     - list() reports retired rows as status 'retired'
#     - tryMembership() never falls through a winding-down retired child to lead
#   agent-team/src/index.ts
#     - TeamService.retireTeammate(caller, targetName)
#   agent-team/tests/{team,projection-events,completion}.spec.ts
#     - slot reclamation, retired row shown + non-addressable, failed-member
#       retire, repeated-retire no-op, non-Lead/unknown/lead/running rejection,
#       replay + absorbing state, wire view keeps the tombstone, stateVersion 5
#   client-ui-agent-team/src/client/TeamAction.tsx + locales.ts
#     - MemberStatus 'retired' renders an inert, idle-dot row ('已退役'/'Retired')
#   tool-agent-team/src/index.ts
#     - MEMBER_VIEW_SCHEMA.status gains 'retired'
#     - new model-facing retire_teammate tool (target, jsonOutput)
#     - policy/list descriptions mention retire, lifetime limit and permanent
#       name reservation
#   tool-agent-team/tests/tool-team.spec.ts
#     - tool set (incl. retired status) + retire_teammate forwarding + policy
#
# Design decisions:
#   * Reuse the existing team/member `phase` field rather than adding an event
#     type (avoids a second write point and a second tombstone collection).
#     The payload version is 2 | 3: retirement edges are written as 3, every
#     existing edge stays 2. An old reader treats a v3 event as unsupported and
#     fails the projection explicitly instead of misreading it.
#   * stateVersion 4 -> 5: the persisted state schema widens its phase domain.
#     A new v5 row is version-mismatched to an old reader, which then refolds
#     the log instead of throwing inside an unguarded stateSchema.parse. New
#     readers refold old v4 caches once, then reuse v5.
#   * Names stay permanently reserved (no renames); only the slot is
#     reclaimed. Retired rows remain durable tombstones so task ownership stays
#     resolvable and the model can still see what existed.
#
# Verification (in a copy of the checkout at /tmp/reclaim-spike/repo):
#   node_modules/.bin/vitest run \
#       packages/experimental/agent-team/tests \
#       packages/experimental/tool-agent-team/tests \
#       packages/experimental/client-ui-agent-team/tests
